From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:04:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/27] Flash Next: the NVFP4 n-gram table through a row cache,
 read ahead of the gather, and an evened prompt tail

Adapts MiaAI-Lab recipe patch 0013 onto 1.2.4: TF_FLASHNEXT_GATHER_READ=pread reads an NVFP4 table's rows into a
direct-mapped cache by up to TF_FLASHNEXT_GATHER_THREADS parked readers (O_DIRECT where the file system allows it,
so the page cache is left to the weights), TF_FLASHNEXT_DRAFT_AHEAD=1 asks for a drafted token's rows while the
head drafts the next one, TF_FLASHNEXT_WARM_AHEAD=1 asks for the next prompt chunk's rows while the chunk before
it runs, and TF_FLASHNEXT_PREFILL_TAIL evens out a short last prompt chunk (two chunks of about equal rows, each
past the prompt expert tiles' 1,024). The rows are the mapping's bytes, so the dequantized rows and every
reply are unchanged. (#9999)
